      </nav>
    </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ea-gc__before ea-gc__before--band" id="before-you-buy">
      <h2 class="ea-gc__h2">Before you buy, <span class="ea-accent">ask</span> the course.</h2>
      <ul role="list">
        <li>What does the gift card pay for: a full round, or a dollar amount?</li>
        <li>Does it pay for a golf cart too, or only the green fee?</li>
        <li>Can it be used on weekends and in the busy season?</li>
        <li>How long is it valid?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>No gift card online? Fill in our free printable card (<a href="https://eagleandash.com/cdn/shop/files/eagle-and-ash-printable-golf-gift-card-round-of-golf.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">US Letter</a> · <a href="https://eagleandash.com/cdn/shop/files/eagle-and-ash-printable-golf-gift-card-round-of-golf-a4.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A4</a>) and book the round together later.</p>
      <p class="ea-gc__words ea-gc__words-intro"><strong>New to golf? Four words you will meet on course websites:</strong></p>
      <p class="ea-gc__words"><strong>Tee time:</strong> a booked start time for a round. <strong>Green fee:</strong> the charge to play the course. <strong>Pro shop:</strong> the course's own shop, where golfers check in. <strong>Resort guest:</strong> someone staying at the course's hotel.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ea-gc__states">
      {%- render 'ea-golf-states-1' -%}
      {%- render 'ea-golf-states-2' -%}
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="ea-gc__part" aria-labelledby="ea-gc-featured">
    <p class="ea-gc__eyebrow">Bucket list</p>
    <h2 class="ea-gc__h2" id="ea-gc-featured">Four famous courses <span class="ea-accent">anyone</span> can play.</h2>
    <ul class="ea-gc__cards" role="list">
      <li class="ea-gc__card">
        <a class="ea-gc__photo" href="#state-wisconsin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
          <img src="{{ 'ea-golf-whistling.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800">
          <span class="ea-gc__label">Wisconsin</span>
        </a>
        <h3 class="ea-gc__h3"><a href="#state-wisconsin">Whistling Straits</a></h3>
        <p class="ea-gc__sub">The Straits Course</p>
        <p>It hosted the PGA Championship in 2004, 2010 and 2015, and the 43rd Ryder Cup. No. 10 on GOLF&#x27;s Top 100 Courses You Can Play 2024-25.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="ea-gc__card">
        <a class="ea-gc__photo" href="#state-florida" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
          <img src="{{ 'ea-golf-sawgrass.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800">
          <span class="ea-gc__label">Florida</span>
        </a>
        <h3 class="ea-gc__h3"><a href="#state-florida">TPC Sawgrass</a></h3>
        <p class="ea-gc__sub">THE PLAYERS Stadium Course</p>
        <p>Home of THE PLAYERS Championship and its island-green 17th hole. Without a hotel stay, tee times open 14 days ahead.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="ea-gc__card">
        <a class="ea-gc__photo" href="#state-south-carolina" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
          <img src="{{ 'ea-golf-kiawah.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800">
          <span class="ea-gc__label">South Carolina</span>
        </a>
        <h3 class="ea-gc__h3"><a href="#state-south-carolina">The Ocean Course</a></h3>
        <p class="ea-gc__sub">Kiawah Island Golf Resort</p>
        <p>It hosted the 1991 Ryder Cup and the 2012 and 2021 PGA Championships. Open all year; golfers not staying at the resort book up to 60 days ahead.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="ea-gc__card">
        <a class="ea-gc__photo" href="#state-washington" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
          <img src="{{ 'ea-golf-chambers.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800">
          <span class="ea-gc__label">Washington</span>
        </a>
        <h3 class="ea-gc__h3"><a href="#state-washington">Chambers Bay</a></h3>
        <p class="ea-gc__sub">University Place</p>
        <p>Host of the 2015 U.S. Open, the first U.S. Open in the Pacific Northwest. Open all year; tee times open 90 days ahead.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>


  <section class="ea-gc__part ea-gc__about" aria-labelledby="ea-gc-chosen">
    <h2 class="ea-gc__h2" id="ea-gc-chosen">How we <span class="ea-accent">chose</span>.</h2>
    <ul class="ea-gc__rules" role="list">
      <li><h3 class="ea-gc__rule-title">Public golfers welcome</h3><p>Every course here takes public golfers. Private clubs are left out: only their members and guests can play, so a gift card could not be used. Where a hotel stay is required, the course is marked.</p></li>
      <li><h3 class="ea-gc__rule-title">Our own checks</h3><p>We started from public rankings (Golfweek's Best 2026 and GOLF Magazine's Top 100 Courses You Can Play 2024-25), then left out every course a gift buyer cannot use: private clubs, courses without a way to give a round, courses closed this year. Our own search added 13 courses that neither ranking lists, each for a story worth telling: Scottish sheep on the fairways in Tennessee, the Wyoming course where the world-record 579-yard drive was hit, a Montana course that was also the town's emergency airstrip. For every course we checked who can play, how to give a round and, where published, the booking window and the season. Where a course sells gift cards online, we read the card's own page to see whether it pays for golf or only for the shop. Each reason names its source.</p></li>
      <li><h3 class="ea-gc__rule-title">Nobody paid to be here</h3><p>No course pays to be on this list. Booking windows, seasons and gift cards come from each course's own website, checked on 11 and 12 November 2026. They change, so check the course's site before you buy.</p></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="ea-gc__credits">Photos from Wikimedia Commons:
      Whistling Straits by Specialkboyle (Public domain, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Whistling_Straits_golf_course,_far_shot.jpg" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">source</a>); TPC Sawgrass, 17th hole by unknown author (Public domain, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TournamentPlayersClub_Sawgrass17thHole.jpg" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">source</a>); Kiawah Island, Ocean Course by Umc1640F (CC0, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kiawah_Island_Golf_Course.jpg" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">source</a>); Chambers Bay by Atomic Taco from Seattle, WA, USA (CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chambers_Bay_Golf_Course_(17998597488).jpg" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">source</a>).
    </p>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}
